  "id": "binary-trial",
  "term": "binary trial",
  "definition": "A binary trial is a trial whose result is recorded in only two possible categories, giving a very coarse measure of behavior. In learning research, this means performance is reduced to a simple two-outcome result rather than capturing the fuller details of what the animal did.",
